ds you use in a telephone conversation."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "most"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the majority or a lot of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It\u2018s the most popular pizza place in town."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Rome"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the capital of Italy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is from Rome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "owner"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who possesses something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hear the owners are from Rome, Italy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "panini"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of sandwich made with Italian bread"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They also make great panini!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to know"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I know you would really like it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le01ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Long O Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A long vowel sound is the same as its name.</br>When a single vowel letter is at the end of a word or syllable, it usually says its long sound. Example: be, go. </br>  When you use two vowels in the same word or syllable, the first vowel is usually long, and the second vowel is usually silent. Example: rope, boat. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Long o sound as in oh, phone, ghost, pillow, roast"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Name your favorite restaurant."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the address of the restaurant."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your favorite meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the meal you don't like (your least favorite)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your answers with your partner."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Restaurantname:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Location:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Favorite meal:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Least favoritemeal:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write the address of my favorite restaurant."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write my favorite meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my answers about the meal with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn3le01ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn3le01ob04re2img05.jpg", "image